    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "when do you use と with this?\n\n危ない　気がする\n危ないと気が付いた　← past tense? correct?\n\n納豆は美味しい＿と＿気が付いた",
      "html": "when do you use と with this?<br/><br/>危ない　気がする<br/>危ないと気が付いた　← past tense? correct?<br/><br/>納豆は美味しい＿と＿気が付いた",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "c5aa2b632270c9cb26fbc634e713690b8261ffd6473de4dd2c0285bbbc1a8485",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "seems to always be preceded with youna~\n ような気がする",
      "html": "seems to always be preceded with youna~<br/> ような気がする",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "bd90399a7e37ef2fa74be4a9d8c5a54643a9a94171d5db4ab387937b5caae047",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "As for the note, 悪い男と思います。is not natural.\nWe say 悪い男_だ_と思います。",
      "html": "As for the note, 悪い男と思います。is not natural.<br/>We say 悪い男_だ_と思います。",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "a4aafb285a4a7a9053e3a1cdb18f39f84c85176cc58643da3bf2553ba91c31da",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Instead of 悪い男のようなような気がする, MIki is correct that one would normally say 悪い男のように思われます。\nIn that example, 気がする would be used in a sense of denial, such as 悪い人のような気がしない。",
      "html": "Instead of 悪い男のようなような気がする, MIki is correct that one would normally say 悪い男のように思われます。<br/>In that example, 気がする would be used in a sense of denial, such as 悪い人のような気がしない。",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "c353f9934304b7f058d5b47cf252e0cf7de57dcd664642533fc021dc070cc5ff",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "悪い　and 危ない are both adjectives, but when the adjetive is used to qulaify a noun, the noun takes + 　のような気\n\n危ない　気がする\n　悪い　気がする\n\nbut\n　悪い男のよう　な　気がする\n\nI find this easiest to remember as \n-like feeling\n-no[you]na 気がする",
      "html": "悪い　and 危ない are both adjectives, but when the adjetive is used to qulaify a noun, the noun takes + 　のような気<br/><br/>危ない　気がする<br/>　悪い　気がする<br/><br/>but<br/>　悪い男のよう　な　気がする<br/><br/>I find this easiest to remember as <br/>-like feeling<br/>-no[you]na 気がする",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "3e1f9d11681c9b7b1f771fb04d0a80fd01613b1c706bf0d42740d720868e6703",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "A line in the notes section of this entry should be changed from:\"verb+のような＋気がする\" to \"verb+ような＋気がする\" (the particle の needs to be dropped)",
      "html": "A line in the notes section of this entry should be changed from:\"verb+のような＋気がする\" to \"verb+ような＋気がする\" (the particle の needs to be dropped)",
